<title>USA: Rite Aid gets consents on Thrifty notes.</title>
<headline>Rite Aid gets consents on Thrifty notes.</headline>
<dateline>CAMP HILL, Pa. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rite Aid Corp said Monday it had received consents from holders of more than 66-2/3 in principal in its tender offer for the 12-1/4 percent senior subordinated notes due 2004 of its Thrifty Payless subsidiary.</p>
<p>The offer expires at midnight January 22, Rite Aid said.</p>
<p>NationsBanc Capital Markets is the dealer-manager for the offer, Rite Aid said.</p>
